--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b2bec28576622e5469ff125d61c4e3a5, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tutorial_2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialogueLines:
  - speakerName: Hacker
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ad771f752afefa244b5c465f7173d61b, type: 3}
    text: Hold up! See the red area?\nThere's a camera over there.
    tags: 
  - speakerName: Hacker
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c4cb55bb1b421e94e9b8af299ed69aa8, type: 3}
    text: Stay out of that unless you want alarms blaring.\nI think it's the model
      that is triggered by loud noises.
    tags: 
  - speakerName: Hacker
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c4cb55bb1b421e94e9b8af299ed69aa8, type: 3}
    text: We need a distraction. Head over to that 3D printer in the corner.
    tags: 
  - speakerName: Hacker
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c4cb55bb1b421e94e9b8af299ed69aa8, type: 3}
    text: Yeah, that chunky machine right there.\nIt's marked in <color=green>green</color>,
      so if you click on it I can hack it remotely.
    tags: 
  - speakerName: Hacker
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c4cb55bb1b421e94e9b8af299ed69aa8, type: 3}
    text: 'I''ll upload a blueprint for something noisy.\nWhen it finish, get close
      to it to pick up the item.

'
    tags: 
  - speakerName: Hacker
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c4cb55bb1b421e94e9b8af299ed69aa8, type: 3}
    text: If the printer is marked in <color=red>red</color> it means you're too
      distant, so be sure to be close enough to make the outline <color=blue>blue</color>
      to make it interactable.
    tags: 
  - speakerName: Hacker
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c4cb55bb1b421e94e9b8af299ed69aa8, type: 3}
    text: if you're colorblind, well... good luck :)
    tags: 
